    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` feature in the Spring PetClinic REST app.\n\n**Behavior:** When `POST /api/owners` receives `sharesHousehold: true` and an existing owner has the same last name and address, the create is now *allowed* (instead of being rejected with 409). Both the new owner and the existing household member are assigned the same stable `householdId`, which is returned on the owner resource. When `sharesHousehold` is not set, the original 409 Conflict behavior is preserved.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `householdId` field (`household_id` column) with getter/setter, plus a `householdKey()` helper that produces the normalized last-name+address key using the same normalization as the existing `sameHouseholdAs`.\n- **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 reworked the household check in `addOwner`: on a household-member match, it 409s only when `sharesHousehold` isn't true; otherwise it calls the new `joinHousehold(...)`, which derives a deterministic UUID from `householdKey()` (so every owner in a household resolves to the same value) and back-fills it onto the existing member.\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `householdId` as a read-only property on the `Owner` response schema (the DTOs are generated from this at build time, so the field flows through MapStruct automatically).\n- **DB schemas** (`db/hsqldb`, `db/h2`, `db/mysql`, `db/postgres`) \u2014 added the `household_id` column to the `owners` table. Tests run under `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema change was required.\n\nThe stable identifier is derived deterministically from the normalized household key, so joiners `b` and `c` in the acceptance test independently compute the same `householdId`. Tests: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
